WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.834
-You look fantastic.
-Thanks so much.

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:05.367
-You know, I'm doing a little
research for our interview here,

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:06.634
and I saw it was ten years ago

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:08.067
that you had
one of your biggest --

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:11.267
One of your first roles,
you were in "Once" on Broadway.

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:13.400
-Yeah. I can't believe
it was ten years ago.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.067
-Ten years ago.
-It's bananas.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:16.167
-That's wild.
-Yeah.

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:17.400
-What do you remember about --

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.901
Because you got nominated
for a Tony for that.

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:20.033
-I did.
-Yeah.

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:22.534
-I was. Yeah! I was!
-Yeah, that's right.

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:23.968
Tell me more about it.

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:26.801
I mean, that's pretty --
-Yeah, it was wild.

00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:29.901
It was, like, beyond anything
I ever could have imagined.

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:32.067
It was really, like,
a golden experience.

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:33.534
-Yeah.
-It was beautiful.

00:00:33.534 --> 00:00:34.734
-Do you get nervous
when famous people

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.767
come to see the show and --
-Terribly. I --

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:38.868
-Do you like to not know?
-I like to not know.

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:41.167
I don't even like to know
when friends of mine are there.

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:42.367
-Right.

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:44.100
-I've gotten a lot chiller
about that now.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.000
Because that's not quite
a chill thing to do.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.200
Be like, "Come see it,
but don't tell me."

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.267
-Yeah, no, you're not
quite doing that.

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:51.501
-Yeah, I don't do that anymore.

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:54.634
But I was really always
very, very nervous.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:58.133
And there was one night where --

00:00:58.133 --> 00:00:59.934
I enter, like, through
the back of the audience

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:01.434
for that show, and I enter --

00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:02.868
So you wait
in the back of the house.

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:05.167
And I saw there was
Secret Service everywhere.

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:08.067
And Beyoncé and Jay-Z
had been coming to see, like,

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.634
a lot of Broadway shows
that week.

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:12.300
And I was like -- [ Chuckles ]
"Here we go."

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.634
Like, I was like, "Well,
they're here. This is great."

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:17.701
-"I'm about to meet them."
-And I was, like, shaking.

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:19.501
And I was like,
"I can't believe they're here.

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:21.133
I can't believe
they're going to see it.

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:22.400
Okay. Alright."

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.167
And I -- We did the show.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:26.000
And then they, quickly, as soon
as it ends, they were like,

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.300
"Come backstage. Someone pretty
special wants to meet you guys."

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.868
And we were all,
like, shaking --

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:33.133
-"Beyoncé just heard me sing.
What am I going to do?"

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:34.300
-"What am I going to do?"

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:37.100
And they were like,
"Okay, guys, come on out.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:38.334
Joe Biden's here."

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:39.534
And I was like...

00:01:39.534 --> 00:01:43.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:44.534
-Yes.

00:01:44.534 --> 00:01:46.467
-Which, you know...

00:01:46.467 --> 00:01:48.334
-Alright.
-It's different.

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:50.100
-It's a different type of --
-It's just different.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.501
-It's a different --
-It's different.

00:01:51.501 --> 00:01:52.767
-It's a different
type of special.

00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:54.067
-It's a different type
of special.

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:56.400
But it's very --
They're pretty different.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.267
-Yeah, did Beyoncé
ever come to see the show?

00:01:58.267 --> 00:01:59.968
-She didn't make it.

00:01:59.968 --> 00:02:01.901
I think she had stuff
she had to do.

00:02:01.901 --> 00:02:03.534
And -- They're busy.

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:06.400
-She never saw "Once" once.
-Yeah, that's right.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.667
She didn't see it once.

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:09.934
-"Nonce."
-She saw it "nonce."

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:11.968
-She saw it "nonce."
-Yeah, she saw it nonce.

00:02:11.968 --> 00:02:13.434
That's okay.

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:16.801
-We asked you if you had
any photos of anyone backstage,

00:02:16.801 --> 00:02:19.133
and you were like, "I guess."

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:21.234
But then, wow,
this is a home run.

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:23.734
-A home run.
-Liza Minnelli came to see you.

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:25.801
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:27.534
-That would freak me out
more than --

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:30.200
-Oh, well, you can see
I'm out of my body.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:34.200
I have -- She came, and I burst
into doves and I couldn't --

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.367
I was beside myself.
Because she's an icon.

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:38.901
-Well, it's Liza Minnelli.
-There's no one greater.

00:02:38.901 --> 00:02:41.133
And her whole entire career --
I mean, I just rewatched

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:43.968
"Arrested Development"
in lockdown,

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:47.100
and her on that is incredible.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.300
-Liza Minnelli is just a --
She's a legend. Amazing.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.067
-And "Arrested Development,"
it's like funny "Succession."

00:02:52.067 --> 00:02:54.367
-[ Laughter ]
-I didn't think about that.

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:56.701
-I mean, "Succession"
is very funny, too,

00:02:56.701 --> 00:02:58.567
but I was like,
"Whoa. There's like some..."

00:02:58.567 --> 00:03:00.267
-I get it. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:03.200
-But she was -- What do you say
to Liza Minnelli?

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.534
-Nothing.

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:07.100
I think I just stammered
and shook and got sweaty and --

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:09.133
-Did everyone freak out?
-She was lovely.

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:12.133
She lined us all up, and
she went up and down the line

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:14.567
and gave everyone, like,
two specific compliments

00:03:14.567 --> 00:03:15.934
while holding their shoulders.

00:03:15.934 --> 00:03:17.367
She held my face.

00:03:17.367 --> 00:03:19.067
I mean, I passed out.
I couldn't believe it.

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:20.567
I don't remember
what she said, but...

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:21.868
-I love Liza Minnelli.
-I know.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.434
-Speaking of icons --
-I was so nervous.

00:03:23.434 --> 00:03:27.133
-There's a thing -- There's
a Cher biopic in the works.

00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:29.934
And I'm excited about that
because I'm a big Cher fan.

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:32.267
-Yeah.
-There's fans on Twitter

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:34.434
that said you should play her
in the biopic.

00:03:34.434 --> 00:03:36.634
-Well -- And I was
very flummoxed by that.

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:38.300
Flattered.
-Flattered and flummoxed?

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:41.300
-Flattered and flummoxed
and bursting into bats.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.534
I couldn't believe it.

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:45.934
Yeah, I realized -- A friend
of mine had told me about it.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:49.601
And I think I had found it
so outlandish and, like, lovely.

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:53.000
But I was like, "Well, no."
Like, she's Cher.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.667
And she's -- I mean,
I worship at her feet, too.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:58.367
But she's like a slinky cat
and I'm like, you know --

00:03:58.367 --> 00:04:00.133
I'm like Don Knotts on a boat.

00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:03.067
[ Laughter ]
You know what I mean?

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:05.167
He's having fun,
but he's windswept.

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:06.934
Do you know what I mean?
It's like --

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:08.634
-You think you're
Don Knotts on a boat

00:04:08.634 --> 00:04:10.234
compared to a slinky cat?
-Yeah.

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:13.300
Like, she's, like, chic
and she's, like, all...

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:14.868
And I just --
-You're Don Knotts...

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:17.334
-On a boat, Jimmy.
Did I stutter?

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:19.234
Yeah.

00:04:19.234 --> 00:04:21.400
-Don Knotts on a boat.
-You know what I mean?

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.167
Like, she's so, like,
"Hey, babe."

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:27.100
Groovy.
-She's unbelievable.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.767
-Unbelievable. I would --
I've seen "Burlesque" 30 times.

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:32.133
-But what if there's
a Don Knotts biopic?

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:33.267
You up for that?

00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:34.801
-Yeah. I'm going to fight.

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:37.934
I'm going to fight
tooth and nail. Yeah.

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:40.200
I'm going to be like,
"Get this. He's on a boat."

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.334
-He has long hair.
-He has long hair.

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:44.300
-And he's gorgeous.
-But he's on a boat.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.834
-"Made for Love" --

00:04:45.834 --> 00:04:48.868
season two premieres
this Thursday on HBO Max.

00:04:48.868 --> 00:04:51.501
I loved the first season.
Everyone loved the first season.

00:04:51.501 --> 00:04:53.801
Congrats on the great reviews.

00:04:53.801 --> 00:04:55.901
How do you set up season two?
Where do we go from here?

00:04:55.901 --> 00:04:58.167
-Well --
-It's trickier.

00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:00.334
-Gosh. It's trickier.

00:05:00.334 --> 00:05:02.234
-Well, your husband's
planted a chip in your brain.

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:03.701
-And he can see everything.

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:05.934
And then I --
My one ally is my father.

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:07.634
I've been gaslit by my husband.

00:05:07.634 --> 00:05:10.901
I'm now gaslighting my father.
It is a comedy.

00:05:10.901 --> 00:05:13.434
But we --
-Ray Romano plays your dad.

00:05:13.434 --> 00:05:15.501
-Ray Romano plays my dad.

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:19.434
But we -- She has to live this,
like, double-life lie now.

00:05:19.434 --> 00:05:21.501
And so it gets very, very murky.

00:05:21.501 --> 00:05:22.701
-Very tricky.
-Very tricky.

00:05:22.701 --> 00:05:24.300
-And you and Billy
are great together.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.634
You guys have worked together?

00:05:25.634 --> 00:05:28.868
-Yeah, we played husband
and wife in this indie film

00:05:28.868 --> 00:05:31.067
a million years ago.

00:05:31.067 --> 00:05:35.467
And it was, like, the first
film -- it was the first job

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:37.334
that I ever just got a
phone call and they were like,

00:05:37.334 --> 00:05:38.601
"They want you
to play this role."

00:05:38.601 --> 00:05:40.033
And I was like, "They do?!"

00:05:40.033 --> 00:05:41.834
Which is great,
but then they don't --

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:43.167
-You didn't have to audition.

00:05:43.167 --> 00:05:44.834
-You don't have to audition,
which is so great.

00:05:44.834 --> 00:05:47.868
But you don't -- Then they don't
know what you're going to do.

00:05:47.868 --> 00:05:49.734
So I showed up --
And I had, like, four lines.

00:05:49.734 --> 00:05:52.567
But I made this whole back story
that she had a pill addiction

00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:54.267
and she wore shoes
that were too small,

00:05:54.267 --> 00:05:57.200
so I would walk weird,
and I had, like, a dress

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:58.968
that I couldn't, like,
turn around in

00:05:58.968 --> 00:06:01.934
so that she'd have to be
like really, like, slurry

00:06:01.934 --> 00:06:04.567
but, like, locked, and it was --

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:06.367
-That's a choice.
-I'll say.

00:06:06.367 --> 00:06:07.968
-For four lines.
-For four lines.

00:06:07.968 --> 00:06:09.334
Yeah, I was like,
"Well, I gotta..."

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:10.801
-Did you talk to the director
or anyone

00:06:10.801 --> 00:06:11.968
before you thought
of this choice?

00:06:11.968 --> 00:06:13.033
-No, no.

00:06:13.033 --> 00:06:14.167
-So you came on set
as this person.

00:06:14.167 --> 00:06:15.501
-So I came on set,
and they were like --

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:17.367
-"Are the cameras are rolling?"
-As the cameras rolling.

00:06:17.367 --> 00:06:18.601
-"Because here comes
this person."

00:06:18.601 --> 00:06:20.200
-And I came up,
and I forget my first line,

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.000
but it was something like,
"Thanks for inviting me

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.400
to the party," or something.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.167
And I was, like,
in a sausage dress being like,

00:06:25.167 --> 00:06:26.667
[Slurring] "Thanks for
inviting me to the pabby."

00:06:26.667 --> 00:06:29.801
And they were like, "Cut! No!"

00:06:29.801 --> 00:06:32.133
[ Laughs ]
And she was like --

00:06:32.133 --> 00:06:33.567
And I remember
the director, like --

00:06:33.567 --> 00:06:35.367
And it was a big party scene,
and she came over

00:06:35.367 --> 00:06:37.834
and she was like,
"What -- What are you doing?"

00:06:37.834 --> 00:06:39.501
-"Are you okay?"
-"Are you okay?"

00:06:39.501 --> 00:06:41.634
-Exactly. They were like,
"Are you nervous?"

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:44.968
And I was like, "No, well,
she has a pill addiction."

00:06:44.968 --> 00:06:47.834
-"My character
has a pill addiction."

00:06:47.834 --> 00:06:50.501
-And I had four lines, and I was
like, "She's like -- Well,

00:06:50.501 --> 00:06:53.100
because she took pills
before the party. I don't know."

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.601
And they were like, "Yeah,
can you just make her Southern?"

00:06:55.601 --> 00:06:57.167
And I was like, "You got it."

00:06:57.167 --> 00:06:58.767
And then they were like,
"Alright, action."

00:06:58.767 --> 00:07:00.434
And I was like, "Howdy!"
-"Hey, y'all!"

00:07:00.434 --> 00:07:01.701
-"Hey, y'all!

00:07:01.701 --> 00:07:04.033
It's, like, really great
being at this party!"

00:07:04.033 --> 00:07:05.734
-Disaster.
-Disaster.

00:07:05.734 --> 00:07:08.801
And then --
And Billy and I got up to --

00:07:08.801 --> 00:07:11.968
We took a train to toon town.
We were getting --

00:07:11.968 --> 00:07:14.400
'Cause then I was like, "Well,
now everything's out the window.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.334
I'm Southern."
I had a whole thing going.

00:07:16.334 --> 00:07:18.367
-Is he Southern, too, now?
-I believe he was.

00:07:18.367 --> 00:07:21.300
I don't remember.
-So he's like, "Hey, y'all."

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.334
-I don't think the picture --
"The picture."

00:07:23.334 --> 00:07:26.200
I just, like, went to the '40s.
The movie. I don't think --

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.734
-"I don't think the picture
ever made it."

00:07:28.734 --> 00:07:31.434
-I didn't think the picture
even took place in the South!

00:07:31.434 --> 00:07:32.734
Yeah, that's right. Yeah.

00:07:32.734 --> 00:07:35.567
It didn't take place
in the South.

00:07:35.567 --> 00:07:37.767
No, and both of us were just
like [Mumbling gibberish]

00:07:37.767 --> 00:07:39.234
"Oh, my Lord!"

00:07:39.234 --> 00:07:41.901
-Can we see that movie?
Can we see you in it?

00:07:41.901 --> 00:07:43.467
-You personally cannot.

00:07:43.467 --> 00:07:45.167
[ Laughter ]
Sorry.

00:07:45.167 --> 00:07:47.100
-I really want to.
-You can't. I'm sorry.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:48.501
-I really can't?
-No.

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:49.801
-I promise you.

00:07:49.801 --> 00:07:51.067
As a friend, I promise you.
-You guys can't.

00:07:51.067 --> 00:07:52.367
-Alright. We can't.

00:07:52.367 --> 00:07:53.767
-Anyone in the room
is not allowed, unfortunately.

00:07:53.767 --> 00:07:56.467
-But we can watch you
in "Made for Love" on HBO Max.

00:07:56.467 --> 00:07:57.801
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:57.801 --> 00:07:59.634
Here's Cristin Milioti
in "Made for Love."

00:07:59.634 --> 00:08:01.000
Take a look.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:04.634
-Hello.
Am I a ghost or something?

00:08:04.634 --> 00:08:07.334
D-Do you people not see me?!

00:08:07.334 --> 00:08:09.767
I know that you know who I am!

00:08:09.767 --> 00:08:12.067
I am Hazel Gogol,
and -- and -- and

00:08:12.067 --> 00:08:15.200
and I am [bleep] allowed
to be down here now

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.834
because I have --

00:08:17.834 --> 00:08:20.033
Because I have this!

00:08:20.033 --> 00:08:23.467
Um, you.

00:08:23.467 --> 00:08:25.334
What do you --
What is your name?

00:08:25.334 --> 00:08:27.834
-Uh, uh, W-William.

00:08:27.834 --> 00:08:30.300
Is that a severed finger?

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:31.667
-Good morning, everyone!

00:08:31.667 --> 00:08:33.434
-Good morning!
-Good morning!

00:08:33.434 --> 00:08:35.334
-Did you need to --

00:08:35.334 --> 00:08:37.300
You need to tell them that
I'm allowed to be down here

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:38.834
and that they can talk to me
like I'm a normal

00:08:38.834 --> 00:08:40.868
[bleep] person because --
because they're all looking

00:08:40.868 --> 00:08:42.234
at me like I'm the boogeyman.

00:08:42.234 --> 00:08:45.234
-Of course. Right, right.
I'll correct this immediately.

00:08:45.234 --> 00:08:46.501
-Wow.

00:08:46.501 --> 00:08:48.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:51.300
How fun.
Cristin Milioti, everybody.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:55.300
Season two of "Made for Love"
premieres Thursday on HBO Max.

